WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.000
Organizations use the CIS Controls to guide security programs,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.840
improve operational practices, identify gaps, prioritize investments,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.000
and communicate security expectations.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.995
The controls can serve as a roadmap for security improvement and program development.

00:00:12.995 --> 00:00:17.905
They help translate security goals into concrete practices that teams can plan and review.

00:00:17.905 --> 00:00:21.995
A team might use the controls to assess current practices, identify missing safeguards,

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:25.000
plan projects, set priorities, and explain why certain activities matter.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.495
This makes the CIS Controls useful for both technical teams and business leaders because

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:32.000
they connect risk reduction to practical work.
